but she scanned twice in that early postpartum period. And she had a mix of first and second time dads, but the sample was too small to really look at group differences. So one of the questions that I would be really curious about is, Did dad sort of like lose more and more volume? Does the brain get more and more streamlined? Or at a certain point, is there more rebound once you have more kids? You've also looked at hormonal changes that can occur in men when they become fathers. Can you tell us more about that research? What are some of the changes that you found and what are the everyday impacts? Yeah, so often when we think about hormones and parenthood, we think about pregnancy and birth, right, which we know are really hormonally rich events. But there's plenty of evidence that we see hormone changes in men as well.
